{#
  T-7.06 — one item in the customer-stories feed. T-7.07 gave it its trigger.

  Usage:
    {% include 'components.stories.story-card' with { story: item, id: 'story-1' } %}

  Parameters:
    story   required — one entry from the story collection
    id      required — the id of the story view this card opens

  WHY THIS IS A PARTIAL AND NOT A LOOP BODY. T-7.07 opens the same item in a
  modal, and the owner's B6 ruling is explicit that the story view is a view of
  *this* item rather than a second thing that happens to look like it. Keeping
  the card in its own file is what let the modal reuse the tag row and the media
  well instead of transcribing them.

  THE CARD BECAME A CONTROL IN T-7.07, AND NOT BEFORE. T-7.06 shipped it inert on
  purpose: pressing a story opens a modal, the modal did not exist, and a card
  that looks pressable and does nothing is worse than a plain image for someone
  who cannot see that it is dead. Now that the modal exists, the media is wrapped
  in a button. **The tags stay outside it** — they are not part of the target,
  which is both the artboard's reading and T-2.15's one-focusable-descendant rule.

  THE ACCESSIBLE NAME IS NOT THE IMAGE'S ALT. Alt is optional here and empty
  means decorative, so a button relying on it would sometimes have no name at
  all. The label is built from the brand when there is one and falls back to the
  generic phrase when there is not.

  THE SHAPE IS A MERCHANT FIELD BECAUSE NOTHING ELSE KNOWS IT. A masonry grid is
  made of images of different heights, and the theme is handed a URL with no
  dimensions attached — so either the box is reserved from a stored ratio or it
  is not reserved at all, and zero CLS is a requirement here, not an aspiration.
  Three shapes cover the artboard; the value feeds `--card-media-ratio`, which
  T-2.15's card shell already reads.
#}
{% set story_ratios = {
    'square':   '1 / 1',
    'portrait': '3 / 4',
    'tall':     '2 / 3'
} %}
{% set story_ratio = story_ratios[story.shape|default('portrait')]|default('3 / 4') %}
{% set story_label = story.brand
    ? trans('theme.stories.open_story_named', { name: story.brand })
    : trans('theme.stories.open_story') %}

<li class="story-card">
    <button type="button"
            class="story-card__trigger"
            data-sheet-open="{{ id }}"
            aria-haspopup="dialog"
            aria-label="{{ story_label }}">
        <div class="card__media story-card__media" style="--card-media-ratio: {{ story_ratio }}">
            <img src="{{ story.image|cdn(400) }}"
             srcset="{{ story.image|cdn(200) }} 200w, {{ story.image|cdn(400) }} 400w, {{ story.image|cdn(600) }} 600w"
             sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 22vw, (min-width: 768px) 30vw, 44vw"
                 alt="{{ story.alt|default('') }}"
                 loading="lazy"
                 decoding="async">
        </div>
    </button>

    {% include 'components.stories.story-tags' with { story: story } only %}
</li>
